            <ArticleTitle>Masking of exercise-induced ST-segment depression by rate-dependent left-axis deviation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1031-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An unexpected high incidence of false negative ST-segment responses to exercise was previously reported for patients with coronary artery disease and abnormal left-axis deviation on their resting electrocardiograms. In the case presented, an exercise-induced, &quot;ischemia&quot; ST-segment depression was masked with the onset of rate-dependent left-axis deviation. The state of the base-line electrocardiogram is an important but often overlooked factor in assessing the incidence of false negative and false positive ST-segment responses to exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
